bbapprove help env — environment variables and exit codes.

Environment
  BBAPPROVE_TOKEN          API token; wins over a 1Password item (help token)
  BBAPPROVE_CONFIG         config file path (also --config); must exist
  BBAPPROVE_REPOSITORY     forge base URL (overrides repository)
  BBAPPROVE_TOKEN_NAME     1Password item name, used only when BBAPPROVE_TOKEN is unset (also --token-name; no default)
  BBAPPROVE_AUTHOR_EMAIL   author the eligibility check requires (overrides author_email)
  BBAPPROVE_UPDATE_REPO    GitHub owner/repo for --outdated and --update (default jesperronn/bbapprove)
  BBAPPROVE_DELETE_SOURCE_BRANCH  true (default) or false: delete the source branch after a merge (overrides delete_source_branch)
  BBAPPROVE_DISALLOW       comma-separated extra disallow items
  BBAPPROVE_DISALLOW_FILE  optional extra disallow file (default disallow.txt in the repo root)
  BBAPPROVE_JOBS           parallel PR fetches and merges (default: CPU count)
  BBAPPROVE_ADAPTER        forge adapter executable (default: the built-in Bitbucket adapter)
  BBAPPROVE_MOUSE          0 turns TUI mouse capture off (same as --no-mouse)
  BBAPPROVE_KITTY          0 stops the TUI requesting the kitty keyboard protocol
  NO_COLOR, FORCE_COLOR  colour only on a terminal; NO_COLOR turns it off and wins, FORCE_COLOR=1 forces it on
  XDG_CONFIG_HOME          base of the config and ignore paths (default ~/.config)
  VISUAL, EDITOR         editor opened by the first-run setup

Adapter side (read by the built-in Bitbucket adapter and by adapters/bitbucket; the core sets BASE_URL, TOKEN_NAME and DELETE_SOURCE_BRANCH from the configuration)
  BBAPPROVE_BASE_URL       forge base URL (required)
  BBAPPROVE_TOKEN_NAME     1Password item for "auth token"
  BBAPPROVE_DELETE_SOURCE_BRANCH  true (default when unset) or false: delete the source branch after a merge
  BBAPPROVE_MERGE_RETRIES  merge retries when the PR went stale or its target moved (default 4)
  BBAPPROVE_RETRY_SLEEP    seconds between retries (default 2)
  BBAPPROVE_TOKEN is required by the "pr" commands (exit 2 when unset).

Exit codes
  0  ok (doctor: warnings allowed; --outdated: up to date)
  1  a failure (doctor: a problem was found; --outdated: a newer release exists)
  2  bad usage (--outdated: could not check)
  127  (launcher) Go is missing and no binary is built
